# Version Management

Each prototype version represents a design iteration. Versions share most pages but diverge on the specific feature under exploration (typically vulnerability reporting and workload views).

## Current Versions

| Version | Directory | Unique Pages | Focus |
|---------|-----------|-------------|-------|
| v1 | `src/pages/` (root) | `CreateReportWizard`, `VulnerabilityReportingPage`, `UserWorkloadVulnerabilities` | MVP with collection-based scoping |
| v2 | `src/pages/v2/` | `V2ReportsPage`, `V2CreateReportWizard`, `V2UserWorkloadVulnerabilities`, `V2SavedFilterDetail` | Saved filter-based scoping |
| v3 | `src/pages/v3/` | `V3ReportsPage`, `V3CreateReportWizard` | Collection + Custom Filters scope (no saved filter scope in wizard) |

## Creating a New Version (vN)

### Step 1: Create the directory

```
src/pages/vN/
```

### Step 2: Add route constants in `src/routes.js`

Add to the bottom of the file:

```js
export const vNRoutes = prefixRoutes('/vN');
```

### Step 3: Create version-specific page files

Fork from the appropriate base version. Name files with the `VN` prefix:

```
src/pages/vN/VNReportsPage.jsx
src/pages/vN/VNCreateReportWizard.jsx
```

### Step 4: Register routes in `src/App.jsx`

1. Import the new route constants and page components at the top:

```jsx
import VNReportsPage from './pages/vN/VNReportsPage';
import VNCreateReportWizard from './pages/vN/VNCreateReportWizard';
import { vNRoutes } from './routes';
```

2. Create a `VNRoutes` function following the same pattern as `V1Routes`, `V2Routes`, `V3Routes`. Use shared pages with `routePrefix="/vN"` and version-specific pages where they differ:

```jsx
function VNRoutes() {
  const r = vNRoutes;
  return (
    <VersionLayout routes={r} version="vN">
      <Routes>
        {/* ... shared routes with routePrefix="/vN" ... */}
        <Route path="main/vulnerabilities/reports" element={<VNReportsPage />} />
        <Route path="main/vulnerabilities/reports/create" element={<VNCreateReportWizard />} />
        {/* ... */}
      </Routes>
    </VersionLayout>
  );
}
```

3. Add the route entry in the `App` component's `<Routes>`:

```jsx
<Route path="/vN/*" element={<VNRoutes />} />
```

### Step 5: Add version card in `src/pages/VersionSelector.jsx`

Add a new `<Card>` to the `<Gallery>`. Follow the existing card pattern:

```jsx
<Card
  isClickable
  isSelectable
  onClick={() => navigate('/vN/main/dashboard')}
  style={{ borderRadius: '12px', overflow: 'hidden', /* ... */ }}
>
  <CardHeader style={{ background: 'linear-gradient(135deg, #COLOR1 0%, #COLOR2 100%)', padding: '24px' }}>
    <Flex justifyContent={{ default: 'justifyContentSpaceBetween' }} alignItems={{ default: 'alignItemsCenter' }} style={{ width: '100%' }}>
      <FlexItem><Label color="COLOR" isCompact>TYPE</Label></FlexItem>
      <FlexItem><Label color="orange" isCompact>New</Label></FlexItem>
    </Flex>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardBody style={{ padding: '24px' }}>
    <CardTitle>
      <Title headingLevel="h2" size="xl" style={{ marginBottom: '12px' }}>
        Version N — Description
      </Title>
    </CardTitle>
    <Content style={{ marginBottom: '20px', color: 'var(--pf-t--global--text--color--subtle)' }}>
      Clear explanation of what this version demonstrates differently.
    </Content>
    <ul style={{ listStyle: 'none', padding: 0, margin: '0 0 20px 0', lineHeight: '2' }}>
      <li>&#x2022; Key feature 1</li>
      <li>&#x2022; Key feature 2</li>
    </ul>
    <Button variant="link" isInline icon={<ArrowRightIcon />} iconPosition="end">
      Launch VN
    </Button>
  </CardBody>
</Card>
```

## Rules

- Shared pages receive `routePrefix="/vN"` prop for internal links
- Version-specific pages do NOT need `routePrefix` (they know their own context)
- Changes to vN pages must NEVER break earlier versions
- The `NavigationSidebar` component reads the `version` prop to adjust nav labels when needed
- All versions share the same API layer, mock data, and component library
- Use a distinct gradient color per version card so they are visually distinguishable

## Which Pages to Fork vs Share

Fork when the feature under exploration changes the page's behavior:
- Report list page (tabs, actions, table columns differ)
- Report creation wizard (scope methods, steps, filter logic differ)
- Workload vulnerabilities view (toolbar, filter behavior differs)

Share everything else (Dashboard, Violations, Compliance, Clusters, Policies, etc.) via the common `src/pages/` directory with `routePrefix` prop.
